      "side": 0,
      "message": "Note that this is a single bpf system call and thus cheap, see bpfGetUidStatsInternal impl.\n\nYou\u0027re not going to gain much by caching this.\n\nThe real problem is the higher level API - which reads all 4 stats (see getEntryValueForType) RX/TX bytes/packets, but then returns just 1 of the 4 values.  So any time someone does want all 4 (which is probably always)... they need to call it 4 times.\n\nIs there a way to fix the API to actually return everything in one go?\nOr perhaps add a newer API?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1984,
        "startChar": 36,
        "endLine": 1984,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "fa467f9cf5050ca46a447669f7277a5a5efdde17",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
